 are scared of  being a beginner i know a lot of my  friends who are now becoming foundation  ear doctors and they are completely  terrified to be a beginner at this thing  or it's even people using chopsticks for  the first time they just find it super  embarrassing and scary to do it i find  it so funny that as adults we look down  on people who are beginners rather than  kind of respecting them because there is  nothing more terrifying and humbling  than being a beginner at all so  terrifying to start something that you  can't control that you don't know how  good or bad you will be at especially  when this thing is done in public all my  life i avoided this completely i only  stuck to things that i knew i was good  at which were science and school i never  actually went out of this and just to  clarify i am definitely 100 projecting  and this is coming because of how much  pressure i have felt in this thing in  general and how much kind of  internalized pressure i had towards  being a beginner but i will say right  now i have never told anyone in real  life that i have a youtube channel i  just find it so scary to say that out  loud in person because i feel as though  i am just like such a beginner at this  thing and it's really really  embarrassing to be a beginner and  sometimes i look back on my videos and i  think that was so amateur and it was so  bad and you know you completely messed  your points up and you didn't say the  thing that you had in mind and it  doesn't come across well and i think oh  this is so so  embarrassing and instead of thinking  that oh yes i am a beginner it's been  only a few months i've been doing this  thing and obviously it will improve and  therefore kind of admitting that out  loud i am the first person who will just  like keep it under wraps unless someone  already knows and then i'll say oh yeah  yeah i do and just like end the  conversation there so i think this is  one of the things that kind of spurred  my frustration but 